WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.477
- Business is creating
something that you believe in.

00:00:05.341 --> 00:00:07.857
Most of the best entrepreneurial ideas

00:00:07.857 --> 00:00:08.809
come out of frustration.

00:00:08.809 --> 00:00:11.355
I think if you can one business well,

00:00:11.355 --> 00:00:12.903
you can run any business.

00:00:12.903 --> 00:00:14.776
- He's the founder of the Virgin Group

00:00:14.776 --> 00:00:17.222
which controls over 400 companies.

00:00:17.222 --> 00:00:19.428
The Virgin brand grew rapidly in the 1980s

00:00:19.428 --> 00:00:22.098
as he setup the Virgin
Atlantic Airline Company.

00:00:22.098 --> 00:00:24.575
In 2016, Forbes listed his net worth as

00:00:24.575 --> 00:00:26.595
five point two billion dollars.

00:00:26.595 --> 00:00:28.785
He's Richard Branson,
and here's my take on his

00:00:28.785 --> 00:00:30.991
top 10 rules for success, volume two.

00:00:30.991 --> 00:00:32.712
Rule number two is my personal favorite

00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:34.327
and I'm curious to figure out which one

00:00:34.327 --> 00:00:35.363
you guys like the best.

00:00:35.363 --> 00:00:36.642
Also guys, as you're watching,

00:00:36.642 --> 00:00:37.475
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:37.475 --> 00:00:40.016
please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:00:40.016 --> 00:00:42.501
Put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:43.422
by your sharing.

00:00:43.422 --> 00:00:45.117
And also, when you write it down,

00:00:45.117 --> 00:00:47.966
you're much more likely to
lock it in for yourself too.

00:00:47.966 --> 00:00:49.042
Enjoy.

00:00:49.042 --> 00:00:52.125
(dramatic crescendo)

00:00:53.957 --> 00:00:56.540
(upbeat music)

00:01:02.021 --> 00:01:04.769
- I think the important
thing to think about business

00:01:04.769 --> 00:01:07.889
is that business isn't really business.

00:01:07.889 --> 00:01:12.777
Business is creating
something that you believe in.

00:01:12.777 --> 00:01:16.132
The most successful
entrepreneurs are people

00:01:16.132 --> 00:01:20.242
like Larry Page and Sergey who
had an idea in their garage,

00:01:20.242 --> 00:01:24.010
and felt they could create
something called Google.

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:28.527
In all of these examples,
they are filling a niche

00:01:28.527 --> 00:01:32.694
in different areas and just
making living, for most people,

00:01:33.649 --> 00:01:35.817
a lot more pleasant than it was before.

00:01:35.817 --> 00:01:38.051
I think it's mistake when
people think of business,

00:01:38.051 --> 00:01:40.280
that they're ringing up a till in a shop.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.418
For most entrepreneurs,
business is very creative

00:01:43.418 --> 00:01:45.346
and a great adventure.

00:01:45.346 --> 00:01:48.238
I think if you believe
in what you're doing,

00:01:48.238 --> 00:01:52.071
many people will tell
you why you're mistaken,

00:01:53.777 --> 00:01:55.399
why it will never work,

00:01:55.399 --> 00:01:58.295
but if you really believe
passionately in what you're doing,

00:01:58.295 --> 00:02:03.057
just keep going, keep
pushing on, keep pushing on

00:02:03.057 --> 00:02:05.076
until you either succeed

00:02:05.076 --> 00:02:09.243
or at least you realize that
it's just not going to happen.

00:02:11.818 --> 00:02:14.083
And then if you don't succeed,

00:02:14.083 --> 00:02:16.666
pick yourself up and try again.

00:02:17.787 --> 00:02:21.287
And ultimately, if you're that determined,

00:02:22.831 --> 00:02:24.652
you will succeed in life.

00:02:24.652 --> 00:02:28.819
And if you don't, you'll
have a lot of fun trying.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:33.658
I started literally in a really small way.

00:02:33.658 --> 00:02:37.575
Like handing out leaflets
outside concert halls

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.635
and selling music.

00:02:41.635 --> 00:02:44.436
Getting the money in from the leaflets

00:02:44.436 --> 00:02:46.807
and then sending the music out.

00:02:46.807 --> 00:02:48.461
Just one thing led on to another.

00:02:48.461 --> 00:02:51.668
So, you don't have to
dream big straight away.

00:02:51.668 --> 00:02:56.622
Just try to get the nuts and
bolts of your business going.

00:02:56.622 --> 00:02:59.284
Whatever job you're doing in life,

00:02:59.284 --> 00:03:01.689
if you're a switchboard operator,

00:03:01.689 --> 00:03:05.556
if you're cleaning the
floors of a building,

00:03:05.556 --> 00:03:09.305
if you're, I don't know,
collecting eggs for an incubator,

00:03:09.305 --> 00:03:10.299
or whatever it is,

00:03:10.299 --> 00:03:14.741
if you're positive about
the job you're doing,

00:03:14.741 --> 00:03:17.997
you're going to be a much happier person

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:21.571
and the people around you are
going to be a lot happier.

00:03:21.571 --> 00:03:25.396
And it's likely that you won't
forever be a cleaning lady

00:03:25.396 --> 00:03:28.289
because you're smiling,
because you're happy,

00:03:28.289 --> 00:03:31.572
people will promote you and you'll go on

00:03:31.572 --> 00:03:34.065
and do great things in life.

00:03:34.065 --> 00:03:37.556
So I think a positive
attitude is essential in life,

00:03:37.556 --> 00:03:39.855
whatever your position.

00:03:39.855 --> 00:03:41.271
- [Interviewer] Looks like you always go

00:03:41.271 --> 00:03:42.872
out of your comfort zone, right?

00:03:42.872 --> 00:03:44.908
Coming onto an island that
was completely deserted,

00:03:44.908 --> 00:03:46.178
no fresh water.

00:03:46.178 --> 00:03:48.020
You didn't even have the money to buy it.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.234
And now you're sleeping
on a tent on the beach

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:53.077
trying to figure out how
to get fresh water here.

00:03:53.077 --> 00:03:55.729
You do that often, you
did it with the airline.

00:03:55.729 --> 00:03:58.593
- I was just somebody that
experienced the bad experience

00:03:58.593 --> 00:04:00.446
of traveling on airlines.

00:04:00.446 --> 00:04:03.260
I was actually trying to get to the BVI,

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:05.513
the British Virgin Islands,
one day from Puerto Rico

00:04:05.513 --> 00:04:07.881
and the same lovely
lady was waiting for me.

00:04:07.881 --> 00:04:09.236
And I'd been away for three weeks

00:04:09.236 --> 00:04:12.569
and American Airlines bumped the flight.

00:04:13.894 --> 00:04:15.290
And so I went to the back of the airport,

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.457
I hired a plane, I hired a blackboard.

00:04:19.764 --> 00:04:23.597
I wrote Virgin Airlines
one way $29 to the BVI

00:04:25.345 --> 00:04:27.122
and went around all the
people who'd been bumped

00:04:27.122 --> 00:04:28.306
and I filled my first plane.

00:04:28.306 --> 00:04:31.642
And that got me thinking
that airlines do bump people.

00:04:31.642 --> 00:04:35.763
They don't care about you or
me particularly, in the air.

00:04:35.763 --> 00:04:37.915
So I then rang up Boeing and said,

00:04:37.915 --> 00:04:40.123
"Do you have any secondhand 747s?"

00:04:40.123 --> 00:04:40.956
- No kidding?

00:04:40.956 --> 00:04:42.531
It was literally that you
just sat in the airport

00:04:42.531 --> 00:04:44.273
and said, "I'm starting
an airline right now

00:04:44.273 --> 00:04:45.106
"because I'm frustrated."

00:04:45.106 --> 00:04:45.939
- Exactly.

00:04:45.939 --> 00:04:49.206
And I think most of the
best entrepreneurial ideas

00:04:49.206 --> 00:04:50.593
come out of frustration.

00:04:50.593 --> 00:04:54.014
I think if you're
frustrated about something,

00:04:54.014 --> 00:04:57.408
the best way of sorting it
out is get out and do it.

00:04:57.408 --> 00:04:59.210
And you've got yourself a business.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.558
Life is short, life should
be fun, and it should be fun,

00:05:01.558 --> 00:05:03.808
and it should be fun, not--

00:05:04.733 --> 00:05:07.290
you know if the chairman of
the company is having fun,

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:10.382
if you go to a party
and I let my hair down,

00:05:10.382 --> 00:05:12.479
and I'm the first to be
thrown in the swimming pool,

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:15.592
and I'm not just standing
in the corner of the room

00:05:15.592 --> 00:05:17.872
sipping sherry or something,

00:05:17.872 --> 00:05:18.705
then everybody will have a laugh,

00:05:18.705 --> 00:05:19.809
and everybody will have fun.

00:05:19.809 --> 00:05:21.396
If you're the chairman of the company,

00:05:21.396 --> 00:05:22.949
be the first to dance on the table.

00:05:22.949 --> 00:05:25.237
Just get everybody else
up dancing on the table.

00:05:25.237 --> 00:05:28.069
Make sure the party's a laugh.

00:05:28.069 --> 00:05:29.986
So play hard, work hard

00:05:32.473 --> 00:05:35.640
and follow certain principles in life.

00:05:38.359 --> 00:05:40.684
Love people, make sure you
make a positive difference

00:05:40.684 --> 00:05:42.456
in this world while you're on it.

00:05:42.456 --> 00:05:44.088
Over the next five years,

00:05:44.088 --> 00:05:47.368
we plan to take on the banking community.

00:05:47.368 --> 00:05:49.407
We plan to take on the cosmetics industry.

00:05:49.407 --> 00:05:52.336
We plan to take on the clothing industry.

00:05:52.336 --> 00:05:55.057
And telecommunications, and
one or two other industries,

00:05:55.057 --> 00:05:57.356
and see whether we can give
them a run for their money

00:05:57.356 --> 00:06:00.312
and do it slightly differently
than it's been done before.

00:06:00.312 --> 00:06:03.062
- Why do you think you can do it?

00:06:04.086 --> 00:06:05.390
- Mainly because I think we've got

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:07.266
a fantastic team of people.

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.310
We attract good people.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:11.018
- And their skills are translatable

00:06:11.018 --> 00:06:12.683
to whatever the industry is?

00:06:12.683 --> 00:06:16.914
It's creativity, it's risk
orientation, it's what?

00:06:16.914 --> 00:06:19.422
- I think if you can
run one business well,

00:06:19.422 --> 00:06:20.984
you can run any business.

00:06:20.984 --> 00:06:23.963
And if you know that
what matters in business

00:06:23.963 --> 00:06:27.339
is a good team of people,
well motivated team of people,

00:06:27.339 --> 00:06:31.298
incentivized well, given
a lot of freedom to go out

00:06:31.298 --> 00:06:35.957
and prove themselves, you can
pretty well achieve anything.

00:06:35.957 --> 00:06:39.874
The key to I think being
a good business leader

00:06:41.417 --> 00:06:43.826
is how good you are with people.

00:06:43.826 --> 00:06:47.743
I think if you can
genuinely care about people,

00:06:48.843 --> 00:06:50.464
and not just your fellow directors,

00:06:50.464 --> 00:06:53.412
but the cleaning lady,
the switchboard operator,

00:06:53.412 --> 00:06:56.162
everybody throughout the company.

00:06:58.745 --> 00:07:01.578
if you praise and don't criticize,

00:07:02.874 --> 00:07:04.624
people will flourish.

00:07:06.791 --> 00:07:09.965
So I think it's really your people skills

00:07:09.965 --> 00:07:11.965
that will set you apart.

00:07:15.299 --> 00:07:18.606
And I don't think that
could be overemphasized.

00:07:18.606 --> 00:07:22.357
I think you've just got to, you know,

00:07:22.357 --> 00:07:25.068
if I'm on a Virgin plane,
I would make sure that

00:07:25.068 --> 00:07:28.855
I always have a notebook
in my back pocket,

00:07:28.855 --> 00:07:30.837
make sure I get out and
talk to all the staff.

00:07:30.837 --> 00:07:35.004
If they've got issues, make
sure I don't just hear the issue

00:07:35.994 --> 00:07:37.310
and not write it down.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:39.276
Make sure those issues get written down.

00:07:39.276 --> 00:07:40.348
Talk to the passengers.

00:07:40.348 --> 00:07:42.009
If they've got issues,

00:07:42.009 --> 00:07:44.137
make sure those issues get written down.

00:07:44.137 --> 00:07:46.257
I honestly just don't
think about mistakes,

00:07:46.257 --> 00:07:47.616
but let me see if I can try.

00:07:47.616 --> 00:07:49.736
I just like to if I make a mistake,

00:07:49.736 --> 00:07:52.831
I put it behind me and
I just move forward.

00:07:52.831 --> 00:07:54.589
- That's what I thought.

00:07:54.589 --> 00:07:55.422
- But--

00:07:57.848 --> 00:07:58.681
- But,

00:08:02.818 --> 00:08:06.294
yes there have been musical bands

00:08:06.294 --> 00:08:10.297
that I've missed trying
to sign like Dire Straits.

00:08:10.297 --> 00:08:11.860
There have been companies

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:13.361
that have falling flat on their face,

00:08:13.361 --> 00:08:14.778
like Virgin Cola.

00:08:17.542 --> 00:08:21.709
You know, but that's just
part of, that just part of

00:08:25.827 --> 00:08:27.246
being an entrepreneur.

00:08:27.246 --> 00:08:29.589
You're going to have these
things happening all the time.

00:08:29.589 --> 00:08:31.682
So, I don't really see them as mistakes.

00:08:31.682 --> 00:08:35.765
They're just, you know,
if you're an entrepreneur

00:08:36.747 --> 00:08:38.971
some things are not going to go right.

00:08:38.971 --> 00:08:41.754
Some things are going to go right.

00:08:41.754 --> 00:08:44.671
(bright pop music)

00:08:46.166 --> 00:08:47.061
(cheering)

00:08:47.061 --> 00:08:47.953
- Tea, coffee, or me?

00:08:47.953 --> 00:08:50.203
(laughing)

00:08:54.842 --> 00:08:58.893
- Ladies and gentlemen, if
I could introduce to you

00:08:58.893 --> 00:09:02.427
Air Asia's newest crew
Sir Richard Branson.

00:09:02.427 --> 00:09:05.927
(cheering and applauding)

00:09:07.734 --> 00:09:08.786
(laughing)

00:09:08.786 --> 00:09:10.619
- He can't look at me.

00:09:11.919 --> 00:09:14.751
They're going to teach
me everything to do.

00:09:14.751 --> 00:09:16.295
This outfit is not working.

00:09:16.295 --> 00:09:19.269
(laughing)

00:09:19.269 --> 00:09:20.673
What do you think about the legs?

00:09:20.673 --> 00:09:23.506
Come on, they're not bad are they?

00:09:24.389 --> 00:09:25.222
Oh Tony.

00:09:25.222 --> 00:09:26.226
Stop it. Stop it.

00:09:26.226 --> 00:09:28.476
(laughing)

00:09:29.891 --> 00:09:32.391
I'm always picking the answer.

00:09:35.359 --> 00:09:37.609
(cheering)

00:10:09.312 --> 00:10:10.783
- [Tony] Open the door.

00:10:10.783 --> 00:10:12.703
(laughing)

00:10:12.703 --> 00:10:13.620
- [All] Oh.

00:10:15.669 --> 00:10:16.918
(tape rewinding)

00:10:16.918 --> 00:10:17.751
Oh.

00:10:22.821 --> 00:10:25.071
(laughing)

00:10:27.886 --> 00:10:30.886
- We've got to get him out of there.

00:10:34.704 --> 00:10:36.287
I didn't say hello.

00:10:47.091 --> 00:10:48.591
I've not meant to.

00:11:00.353 --> 00:11:01.999
- Hello.
- Hello.

00:11:01.999 --> 00:11:02.832
- Hi.

00:11:08.662 --> 00:11:11.403
- ♫ Happy Birthday to you.

00:11:11.403 --> 00:11:12.236
Whoo.

00:11:22.404 --> 00:11:24.654
(laughing)

00:11:25.879 --> 00:11:27.439
- Hang on a minute.

00:11:27.439 --> 00:11:28.825
Okay.

00:11:28.825 --> 00:11:29.900
- Thank you very much.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:31.334
You can put it down please.

00:11:31.334 --> 00:11:32.167
- Okay.

00:11:35.655 --> 00:11:37.905
(laughing)

00:11:59.476 --> 00:12:00.835
Well hi, this is Richie.

00:12:00.835 --> 00:12:02.623
I just want to say thank you very much

00:12:02.623 --> 00:12:03.456
for flying with us today.

00:12:03.456 --> 00:12:06.526
It's been delightful working
with all the cabin crew.

00:12:06.526 --> 00:12:09.865
And I just want to say thank you very much

00:12:09.865 --> 00:12:11.374
for flying Air Asia X

00:12:11.374 --> 00:12:13.347
and we hope to see you back again soon.

00:12:13.347 --> 00:12:15.903
I don't think I'm going to be allowed

00:12:15.903 --> 00:12:18.591
to come back on the plane again (laughs).

00:12:18.591 --> 00:12:19.761
But it's been great fun.

00:12:19.761 --> 00:12:21.314
Thanks very much for being with us.

00:12:21.314 --> 00:12:23.349
Thanks for raising lots and lots and lots

00:12:23.349 --> 00:12:25.715
of money for Starlight.

00:12:25.715 --> 00:12:27.226
And, yeah, thanks a lot.

00:12:27.226 --> 00:12:28.059
See you soon.

00:12:28.059 --> 00:12:29.258
Cheers.

00:12:29.258 --> 00:12:30.694
(applauding)

00:12:30.694 --> 00:12:32.965
- Please give a warm, Malaysian welcome,

00:12:32.965 --> 00:12:36.865
to our new flight crew
Sir Richard Branson.

00:12:36.865 --> 00:12:40.508
(cheering and applauding)

00:12:40.508 --> 00:12:41.493
- Welcome.
- Thank you.

00:12:41.493 --> 00:12:43.815
- Aireen, we won't be hiring him.

00:12:43.815 --> 00:12:46.770
(laughing)

00:12:46.770 --> 00:12:48.020
- Since I own the company,

00:12:48.020 --> 00:12:50.238
Richard will not be hired.

00:12:50.238 --> 00:12:53.155
In fact, right now, I'm firing him.

00:12:55.445 --> 00:12:56.278
- It's great.

00:12:56.278 --> 00:12:59.480
We raised lots of money for
the Starlight Foundation.

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:00.958
We had a wonderful flight.

00:13:00.958 --> 00:13:03.960
And while I'm here, I'd
just like to congratulate

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:07.904
Tony and all the wonderful
team at Air Asia and Air Asia X

00:13:07.904 --> 00:13:10.644
for the incredible job they've done.

00:13:10.644 --> 00:13:14.967
They've transformed
traveling out of Malaysia

00:13:14.967 --> 00:13:16.904
and around Asia.

00:13:16.904 --> 00:13:19.078
And they deserve all the credit for it.

00:13:19.078 --> 00:13:21.566
I always wanted to be an FSS,

00:13:21.566 --> 00:13:25.527
but it looks like I'm
just going to have to

00:13:25.527 --> 00:13:27.268
get back to formality.

00:13:27.268 --> 00:13:29.169
But anyway, thank you
very much for coming out.

00:13:29.169 --> 00:13:30.090
Cheers.

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:33.590
(cheering and applauding)

00:13:45.013 --> 00:13:46.932
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:13:46.932 --> 00:13:48.615
I'd love to know, what did
you think of this video?

00:13:48.615 --> 00:13:50.905
And in general, what do you
think of our Volume Two series?

00:13:50.905 --> 00:13:52.331
Please leave a comment down below.

00:13:52.331 --> 00:13:54.720
I'd also love to know what did
you learn from Richard today?

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:56.393
What was your favorite clip and why?

00:13:56.393 --> 00:13:58.524
What lesson are you going
to immediately apply

00:13:58.524 --> 00:13:59.832
to your life or business?

00:13:59.832 --> 00:14:01.657
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:14:01.657 --> 00:14:02.947
I'm super curious to find out.

00:14:02.947 --> 00:14:04.998
Finally, I wanted to give a
quick shout out to Shimon.

00:14:04.998 --> 00:14:07.003
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:14:07.003 --> 00:14:07.883
Your One Word.

00:14:07.883 --> 00:14:09.789
It really, really, really,
really means a lot to me.

00:14:09.789 --> 00:14:11.545
And I hope you're enjoying your read.

00:14:11.545 --> 00:14:12.590
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:14:12.590 --> 00:14:14.045
I believe in you.

00:14:14.045 --> 00:14:15.746
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:14:15.746 --> 00:14:17.531
and whatever your one word is,

00:14:17.531 --> 00:14:18.862
much love.

00:14:18.862 --> 00:14:19.849
I'll see you soon.

00:14:19.849 --> 00:14:22.932
(dramatic crescendo)

00:14:26.251 --> 00:14:30.377
- I think it's sort of
foolish to spend your life

00:14:30.377 --> 00:14:33.184
not becoming expert at your passions.

00:14:33.184 --> 00:14:34.859
If you're passionate about something,

00:14:34.859 --> 00:14:37.747
you're going to give it your all.

00:14:37.747 --> 00:14:41.624
And, you're going to
enjoy learning about it.

00:14:41.624 --> 00:14:45.152
Whereas if you have no interest in it,

00:14:45.152 --> 00:14:47.891
you're not going to lap it up.

00:14:47.891 --> 00:14:50.432
I was flying from the
British Virgin Island.

00:14:50.432 --> 00:14:54.599
No sorry, from Puerto Rico to
the British Virgin Islands.

00:14:55.723 --> 00:14:57.264
And I was 28 years old

00:14:57.264 --> 00:14:59.838
and I'd been away from
home for three weeks.

00:14:59.838 --> 00:15:03.996
And I had this gorgeous
lady waiting for me.

00:15:03.996 --> 00:15:07.773
And American Airlines announced that

00:15:07.773 --> 00:15:11.260
they're not going to fly to
flight til the next morning.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:12.826
They didn't have enough passengers.

00:15:12.826 --> 00:15:14.484
And I was damned if I was going to wait

00:15:14.484 --> 00:15:15.655
til the next morning.

00:15:15.655 --> 00:15:18.369
And so I went to the back of the airport

00:15:18.369 --> 00:15:19.743
and I borrowed a blackboard.

00:15:19.743 --> 00:15:23.785
And I scribbled Virgin Airlines as a joke.

00:15:23.785 --> 00:15:26.223
$39 one way to the British Virgin Islands

00:15:26.223 --> 00:15:28.822
and went around all the passengers

00:15:28.822 --> 00:15:30.915
and I managed to fill up my first flight.

00:15:30.915 --> 00:15:33.165
(laughing)

00:15:34.195 --> 00:15:35.166
And when I got to the BVI,

00:15:35.166 --> 00:15:37.279
the guy on my left turned to me and said,

00:15:37.279 --> 00:15:38.993
"Sharpen up the service a bit

00:15:38.993 --> 00:15:42.694
"and you could be in
the airline business."

00:15:42.694 --> 00:15:44.111
And the next day,

00:15:46.144 --> 00:15:48.369
anyway the night went well.

00:15:48.369 --> 00:15:50.105
(laughing)

00:15:50.105 --> 00:15:51.272
The next day--

00:15:53.021 --> 00:15:54.383
She's now my wife, 40 years.

00:15:54.383 --> 00:15:55.271
Still, 40 years later.

00:15:55.271 --> 00:15:57.676
- Thank goodness, she might see this.

00:15:57.676 --> 00:16:01.265
- The next day I rang
up Boeing and I said,

00:16:01.265 --> 00:16:03.252
"I'm thinking of going
into the airline business.

00:16:03.252 --> 00:16:06.863
"In fact, I've just had my test flight.

00:16:06.863 --> 00:16:11.028
"Do you have any second
hand 747s for sale?"

00:16:11.028 --> 00:16:13.570
The person who took the phone call,

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:16.848
I thought he was going to
put the phone down on me,

00:16:16.848 --> 00:16:18.855
but he hung on in there.

00:16:18.855 --> 00:16:22.081
So he said, "Well, what
does your company do?"

00:16:22.081 --> 00:16:24.374
And I said, "Well, we're a record company.

00:16:24.374 --> 00:16:26.432
"We've got The Rolling Stones,
we've got The Sex Pistols."

00:16:26.432 --> 00:16:29.755
And he didn't sound very, very--

00:16:29.755 --> 00:16:31.156
Then he said, "What's
the name of the company?"

00:16:31.156 --> 00:16:32.191
And I said, "Virgin."

00:16:32.191 --> 00:16:34.042
There was a long pause and he said,

00:16:34.042 --> 00:16:36.282
"Well look, we'll send
a salesman to see you

00:16:36.282 --> 00:16:37.868
but with a name like Virgin,

00:16:37.868 --> 00:16:41.138
I just hope your airline
goes the whole way."

00:16:41.138 --> 00:16:43.024
(laughing)

00:16:43.024 --> 00:16:44.284
Things that frustrate you,

00:16:44.284 --> 00:16:45.852
and if you think you can do it better,

00:16:45.852 --> 00:16:47.136
then you have a business.

00:16:47.136 --> 00:16:48.219
Get it going.

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:53.953
So I think

00:16:54.995 --> 00:16:59.618
all I can say is don't
get down at the moment.

00:16:59.618 --> 00:17:02.222
All of us did get down at school.

00:17:02.222 --> 00:17:05.130
Look forward to when you leave school

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:07.379
and you can follow your dreams.

00:17:07.379 --> 00:17:09.902
Concentrate on things you love.

00:17:09.902 --> 00:17:13.819
If you love film, or
theater, or arts, you know

00:17:15.005 --> 00:17:16.993
put more effort into that.

00:17:16.993 --> 00:17:19.129
Rather than the things you don't,

00:17:19.129 --> 00:17:20.552
you're not good at.

